\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Let me go, let me go,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Lord, to me Thy presence show!
\par  Thither still my heart is turning,
\par For Thy eav'nly courts is yearning,
\par  There Thy perfect peace to know.
\par And to be within thy throne.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sweetest light, sweetest light,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Sun that scatt'rest clouds in flight.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 O, when shall I come before Thee
\par when shall I wish saints adore Thee
\par dwell there in thy presence bright
\par To see you in Thou great light.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Ah, how clear, ah, how clear
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Ring the angel voices there,
\par While my soul for wings is sighing,
\par \pard\li135\sl190\slmult0  Wings O'er vale and mountain flying,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 There in Zion to appear.
\par And to get Thou Perfect clear
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When I enter Salem City,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 You celetial City of Gold;
\par It shall be so well with me,
\par And that shall never pass away,
\par It shall be a glorious day,
\par And an everlasting bliss.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  What shall be, what shall be
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 All the joy laid up for me?
\par Lord, I know not eyes are holden,
\par 'Til Jerusalem the golden,
\par In its beauty I shall see
\par At the throne of God for free.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

